# Short, print-friendly links for tap stands, key fobs and QR codes.
#
# A key fob is ~30mm across, so the QR printed on it has to encode as little as
# possible — a long /.netlify/functions/... URL makes a dense QR that scans badly
# at that size. These rewrites give us:
#
#   https://trey.today/t/<locationId>    (was /.netlify/functions/tap?locationId=…)
#   https://trey.today/q/<locationId>    (the printable QR PNG)
#
# 200 = rewrite, not redirect: the short URL stays in the address bar AND the
# function still runs, counts the tap and forwards to Google. The original long
# URLs keep working, so anything already printed or programmed is unaffected.

# FIXED 15 Aug. These previously read:
#     /t/*   /.netlify/functions/tap?locationId=:splat      200
#     /q/*   /.netlify/functions/tap-qr?locationId=:splat   200
# The rewrite DID fire — the function ran — but Netlify did not substitute
# :splat into the destination's QUERY STRING, so locationId arrived empty and
# every short link answered "this tap link isn't set up correctly". Since this
# is the form admin.html writes to NFC tags and encodes into the printed QR,
# every tag and every QR minted from the admin panel was dead on arrival.
# Named placeholders are the documented way to do this. Belt and braces: both
# functions now ALSO read the id straight from the request path, so already
# programmed tags keep working even if this rule misbehaves again.
/t/:id   /.netlify/functions/tap?locationId=:id      200
/q/:id   /.netlify/functions/tap-qr?locationId=:id   200

# The login-free inbox as ONE opaque token: /i/<32 hex key><locationId>
#
# Added 17 Aug so the activation WhatsApp can offer a BUTTON rather than pasting
# a naked URL into the message body. A WhatsApp URL-button variable has to be a
# plain suffix on a fixed base, and the long form carries two query parameters
# (`loc` and `k`), which Meta rejects. Same single-token shape approve.js and
# google-post.js already use.
#
# The long /.netlify/functions/inbox?loc=…&k=… form still works, so every link
# already sent keeps working and nothing has to be reissued.
/i/:t    /.netlify/functions/inbox?r=:t              200
